  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "| $y$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n\nCompute $P(-1<Y\\le 1)$ given that the random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y)$ shown in the table above.\n\n$P(-1<Y\\le 1)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1<Y\\le 1) & =P(Y\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =P(Y=0)+P(Y=1) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
